diff --git a/docs/CHIKLETS.md b/docs/CHIKLETS.md
index 235c36a..ff142e2 100644
--- a/docs/CHIKLETS.md
+++ b/docs/CHIKLETS.md
@@ -144,6 +144,43 @@ The left side is the Foreman job-template input name. The right side is the Chik
 
 Every `input_map` source must exist in `form_schema.properties`. Invalid Chiklet definitions are rejected when loaded rather than allowing an unmapped or hidden value to reach Foreman.
 
+### Live Foreman input contract
+
+When `FOREMAN_PREFLIGHT_INPUTS_ON_SUBMIT=true` (the production default), Self-Service also resolves the configured Foreman job template and reads its live template inputs before accepting a request. The request is rejected if:
+
+- an `input_map` destination does not exist on the Foreman template; or
+- the Foreman template exposes an unmapped input that is required or has a blank default.
+
+This prevents a blank Foreman input from silently overriding an Ansible role default. The same pre-flight is repeated by the worker immediately before job creation, so a template changed after approval still fails closed without launching Ansible.
+
+Schema defaults are defensively re-applied while building the Foreman payload. For example, if the Chiklet defines:
+
+```json
+"mssql_repo_source": {
+  "type": "string",
+  "enum": ["katello", "microsoft"],
+  "default": "katello"
+}
+```
+
+then `katello` is sent for a mapped `mssql_repo_source` even if an older/incomplete request snapshot contains an empty value.
+
+A Foreman template may intentionally have an input that Self-Service does not control. If that input legitimately has a blank default, explicitly acknowledge it in the Chiklet:
+
+```json
+"foreman": {
+  "job_template_name": "SelfService - Example",
+  "input_map": {
+    "managed_input": "managed_field"
+  },
+  "allow_unmapped_inputs": [
+    "optional_external_input"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Use `allow_unmapped_inputs` sparingly; mapped inputs are preferable because they are visible in the approval snapshot and audit trail.
+
 ## Security
 
 Raw passwords and secret fields are intentionally prohibited from Chiklet forms because submitted values become part of the immutable request/audit history. Pass secret references and resolve the actual secret in Foreman, Ansible Vault, or the organisation's secret-management platform.
